    {
      "id": "BIB2JwIhsEWfyUzgbGuwG",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 287.7251778565713,
      "y": 508.4999999999999,
      "width": 450.9975728273243,
      "height": 854.7965875836121,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#4dabf7",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "ay",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1594074232,
      "version": 1795,
      "versionNonce": 2126985848,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1791182973260,
      "created": 1791172329163,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "* tmux - Terminal Multiplexer \n- manage multiple terminal tasks in a single workspace\n- improves session stability - logs & command execution\n\n* git - artifact version control\n- Multiple agents work on different branches. Git provides\nbranching and version control. GitHub provides collaboration.\n\n* jq - simplify JSON processing\n- automation scripts, CI/CD pipelines, API Integrations\n\n* pgrep - simplifies process discovery in Linux env with low\noverhead.\n\n* ss - analyses network connections efficiently\n\n* lsof - provides deep visibility into files & ports, but it\nconsumes more resources. I use lsof when troubleshooting\nrequires detailed process and file infromation.\n\n* dolt - Git solves version control for database code and\nmigration scripts. Dolt extends the same concepts to the\ndatabase contents themselves. The main benefit appears\nwhen multiple people or AI agents need to experiment with\nor modify data in parallel and later merge approved data\nchanges back into a common baseline.\n\n* bd - to move quickly to a parent directory by name\ninstead of counting directory levels.\n\n* flock - to ensure that only one process executes a critical\noperation at a time.\n- flock provides lightweight process synchronization through\nfile locks and helps prevent race conditions when multiple\nscripts, services or agents access shared resources.\n\n* gh - CLI allows AI agents and developers to automate pull\nrequests, code reviews, issue management, and workflow\nexecution directly from the terminal\n\n* claude - provides the reasoning capability for an AI agent,\nwhile tools such as Git branches, GitHub CLI, Dolt, and\nflock provide safe collaboration, version control, and\nexecution coordination.\n",
      "fontSize": 15.196383779264217,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "* tmux - Terminal Multiplexer \n- manage multiple terminal tasks in a single workspace\n- improves session stability - logs & command execution\n\n* git - artifact version control\n- Multiple agents work on different branches. Git provides branching and version control. GitHub provides collaboration. \n\n* jq - simplify JSON processing\n- automation scripts, CI/CD pipelines, API Integrations\n\n* pgrep - simplifies process discovery in Linux env with low overhead.\n\n* ss - analyses network connections efficiently\n\n* lsof - provides deep visibility into files & ports, but it consumes more resources. I use lsof when troubleshooting requires detailed process and file infromation.\n\n* dolt - Git solves version control for database code and migration scripts. Dolt extends the same concepts to the database contents themselves. The main benefit appears when multiple people or AI agents need to experiment with or modify data in parallel and later merge approved data changes back into a common baseline.\n\n* bd - to move quickly to a parent directory by name instead of counting directory levels.\n\n* flock - to ensure that only one process executes a critical operation at a time.\n- flock provides lightweight process synchronization through file locks and helps prevent race conditions when multiple scripts, services or agents access shared resources.\n\n* gh - CLI allows AI agents and developers to automate pull requests, code reviews, issue management, and workflow execution directly from the terminal\n\n* claude - provides the reasoning capability for an AI agent, while tools such as Git branches, GitHub CLI, Dolt, and flock provide safe collaboration, version control, and execution coordination.\n",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
