      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "* Project / City level Templates?\n* How to configure team and their\nconfigurations?",
      "fontSize": 36,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 6,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "* Project / City level Templates?\n* How to configure team and their configurations?",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
    {
      "id": "LKMrtfV45p0jQnEalikNZ",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 297.82568922997376,
      "y": 1377.5692464185286,
      "width": 364.7629628068526,
      "height": 146.63590982964888,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b0J",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1319602552,
      "version": 179,
      "versionNonce": 385007480,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1791183003401,
      "created": 1791182979607,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Nix provides environment consistency through\ndeclarative specifications of dependencies.\nDocker packages an entire runtime, whereas Nix\nreproducibly constructs the environment from a\nversion-controlled definition. Teams often use\nNix for development environments and Docker\nfor deployment runtimes.",
      "fontSize": 16.75838969481701,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 6,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Nix provides environment consistency through declarative specifications of dependencies. Docker packages an entire runtime, whereas Nix reproducibly constructs the environment from a version-controlled definition. Teams often use Nix for development environments and Docker for deployment runtimes.",
